issue_context.body:
**Describe the bug**
c-files that may not be 100% ACPI-related cannot unconditionally include the `include/zephyr/acpi/acpi.h` header file because it will contain invalid C-code if CONFIG_ACPI is disabled.

**Expected behavior**

acpi.h can be always be unconditionally included, allowing the use of e.g. `IS_ENABLED()` in the code.

**Impact**

Only 100% ACPI-related c-files may include the header file, or then the inclusion as well as any related code needs to be protected by #ifdef guards.

**Additional context**

The two problematic structs in acpi.h are these:
```c
struct acpi_irq_resource {
	uint32_t flags;
	union {
		uint16_t irq;
		uint16_t irqs[CONFIG_ACPI_IRQ_VECTOR_MAX];
	};
	uint8_t irq_vector_max;
};

struct acpi_mmio_resource {
	struct acpi_reg_base reg_base[CONFIG_ACPI_MMIO_ENTRIES_MAX];
	uint8_t mmio_max;
};
```

They're used by these APIs:
```c
int acpi_device_irq_get(struct acpi_dev *child_dev, struct acpi_irq_resource *irq_res);

int acpi_device_mmio_get(struct acpi_dev *child_dev, struct acpi_mmio_resource *mmio_res);
```

The Kconfig dependency could be removed by removing the arrays from the structs and changing the APIs so that the callers provide the array storage and the array sizes.
